WEBVTT

00:00:09.940 --> 00:00:15.750
Full energy is troubled because there's no place to go

00:00:16.210 --> 00:00:22.030
A slight shake destroys boredom

00:00:22.320 --> 00:00:28.170
I Ride, On the White Line  OH, OH, OH

00:00:28.420 --> 00:00:34.240
Sit Down  At the place I trust  OH, OH, OH

00:00:34.430 --> 00:00:37.540
We can go even if we're lost

00:00:37.770 --> 00:00:43.650
Everyone receives freedom and passion

00:00:44.040 --> 00:00:49.850
We were born to shine, and our journey continues

00:00:50.180 --> 00:00:56.060
Your soul is the key that supports our uncertain days

00:00:56.350 --> 00:01:02.000
The best growth creates an unstoppable WILD DRIVE

00:01:02.420 --> 00:01:08.270
We still quietly knock on the door

00:01:17.990 --> 00:01:24.000
Deck Master Judge Man's Verdict

00:01:39.580 --> 00:01:45.580
Losing to Yugi Muto is one thing, but losing to that amateur too?

00:01:45.580 --> 00:01:48.020
They're useless.

00:01:49.550 --> 00:01:51.960
I am terribly sorry.

00:01:51.960 --> 00:01:55.030
You have every right to be angry.

00:01:55.370 --> 00:01:56.820
Ooka.

00:01:57.740 --> 00:01:59.650
Don't get the wrong idea.

00:01:59.650 --> 00:02:03.000
I'm not angry.  Just disgusted.

00:02:03.320 --> 00:02:04.740
My apologies.

00:02:05.040 --> 00:02:09.510
The Big Five worked behind-the-scenes to support Kaiba Corporation.

00:02:09.510 --> 00:02:16.600
I was hoping you'd serve me well, but it seems I've miscalculated.

00:02:16.600 --> 00:02:18.500
I no longer need you.

00:02:18.730 --> 00:02:20.850
Give up on getting real bodies.

00:02:20.850 --> 00:02:23.720
P-Please wait, Mr. Noa!

00:02:23.720 --> 00:02:30.440
Among The Big Five, those two were the most useless!

00:02:31.360 --> 00:02:33.760
But I'm not like them.

00:02:33.760 --> 00:02:35.720
Please give me a chance.

00:02:35.720 --> 00:02:39.600
I promise to meet your expectations.

00:02:39.600 --> 00:02:41.170
You're very confident.

00:02:41.480 --> 00:02:47.610
Allow me to defeat them so that I can get a real body.

00:02:49.920 --> 00:02:53.320
Fine.  I'll give you another chance.

00:02:54.960 --> 00:02:56.490
Leave it to me.

00:02:57.520 --> 00:02:59.140
He thinks he's so smooth.

00:02:59.350 --> 00:03:01.320
He can do whatever he likes.

00:03:01.320 --> 00:03:06.640
You're responsible for the weak ones, so just deal with them.

00:03:11.160 --> 00:03:15.080
The one I want... is him.

00:03:16.310 --> 00:03:18.120
Battle Ship, do you copy?

00:03:18.120 --> 00:03:19.220
Battle Ship?

00:03:19.720 --> 00:03:21.750
No good, big brother?

00:03:22.150 --> 00:03:28.190
Yeah.  We have to escape from this annoying virtual world first.

00:03:35.680 --> 00:03:38.730
Hey Shizuka!  Yugi!

00:03:38.730 --> 00:03:44.400
Damn.  I don't know where my friends are, and The Big Five haven't shown up either.

00:03:44.750 --> 00:03:46.910
What's going on?

00:03:48.000 --> 00:03:52.080
I don't have time to waste here!

00:03:57.510 --> 00:03:59.280
What's this?

00:04:00.440 --> 00:04:02.290
A door inside a wall?

00:04:03.670 --> 00:04:05.170
How suspicious.

00:04:08.880 --> 00:04:11.030
It's the Battle Ship!

00:04:11.370 --> 00:04:13.600
I'm back in the real world!

00:04:13.600 --> 00:04:14.720
Lucky!

00:04:14.720 --> 00:04:17.300
Maybe everyone's back too.

00:04:17.300 --> 00:04:19.770
Hey Yugi!  Shizuka!

00:04:21.400 --> 00:04:23.860
Seems no one's here.

00:04:25.580 --> 00:04:27.200
That room...

00:04:36.530 --> 00:04:37.560
Mai...

00:04:38.330 --> 00:04:42.830
Enjoy the world of pain that's inside your heart!

00:04:51.970 --> 00:04:53.600
Just wait, Mai.

00:04:53.970 --> 00:04:58.370
I will defeat Marik and wake you up.

00:05:00.280 --> 00:05:00.880
Mai!

00:05:02.880 --> 00:05:04.300
You're awake!

00:05:07.850 --> 00:05:08.790
Mai!

00:05:10.200 --> 00:05:13.400
Too bad.  You're still in the virtual world.

00:05:13.400 --> 00:05:15.730
Sorry to deceive you, Jonouchi.

00:05:16.580 --> 00:05:18.060
You're not Mai!

00:05:18.060 --> 00:05:19.160
Who are you?

00:05:22.910 --> 00:05:24.770
You're one of The Big Five!

00:05:24.770 --> 00:05:26.480
Let me introduce myself.

00:05:26.480 --> 00:05:29.140
I'm one of The Big Five.

00:05:29.140 --> 00:05:35.400
Kaiba Corporation's legal council, Chikuzen Ooka.  Nice to meet you.

00:05:35.850 --> 00:05:37.420
You're a lawyer?

00:05:37.420 --> 00:05:43.600
Yes.  I can change the color black into white if it would profit Kaiba Corporation.

00:05:43.600 --> 00:05:51.200
It's all thanks to me that Kaiba Corporation grew into a large company.

00:05:51.420 --> 00:05:54.770
Huh?  Change black into white?

00:05:54.770 --> 00:05:55.630
I don't get it.

00:05:56.650 --> 00:05:58.120
Sorry.

00:05:58.120 --> 00:06:01.320
That expression was too difficult for you.

00:06:01.320 --> 00:06:04.020
It means that whenever we were sued...

00:06:04.020 --> 00:06:07.910
...we'd be acquitted as long as I was working on the case.

00:06:08.660 --> 00:06:11.160
That's nothing to brag about!

00:06:11.160 --> 00:06:15.020
A lawyer's job is to reveal the truth!

00:06:15.020 --> 00:06:16.070
Truth?

00:06:16.980 --> 00:06:18.970
Let me ask you something.

00:06:18.970 --> 00:06:20.720
What is the truth?

00:06:21.770 --> 00:06:24.160
The truth is something that's true.

00:06:25.600 --> 00:06:26.770
Sorry.

00:06:26.770 --> 00:06:29.570
I've asked you a difficult question again.

00:06:29.570 --> 00:06:31.600
I'll tell you.

00:06:32.140 --> 00:06:35.040
My words are the truth.

00:06:36.450 --> 00:06:38.850
You have an answer for everything!

00:06:38.850 --> 00:06:41.400
You're so annoying, you bogus lawyer!

00:06:41.540 --> 00:06:43.910
I take that as a complement.

00:06:43.910 --> 00:06:47.370
Anyway, I know you want to duel me!

00:06:47.370 --> 00:06:49.220
Let's start already!

00:06:49.220 --> 00:06:50.820
Are you sure?

00:06:50.820 --> 00:06:53.460
I'll get your body if you lose.

00:06:53.770 --> 00:06:56.220
That sounds disgusting!

00:06:56.440 --> 00:07:01.000
I have to defeat you to escape this virtual world!

00:07:01.000 --> 00:07:02.070
So that's what I'll do!

00:07:02.070 --> 00:07:03.280
Understood.

00:07:03.280 --> 00:07:04.500
Let's begin.

00:07:14.370 --> 00:07:16.810
This is our duel field.

00:07:18.250 --> 00:07:20.170
Where am I?

00:07:21.150 --> 00:07:23.940
This is a courtroom.

00:07:23.940 --> 00:07:28.330
I'm the judge.  You're the defendant.

00:07:28.700 --> 00:07:30.490
I'm the defendant?

00:07:30.490 --> 00:07:34.540
Usually, it's my job to defend the defendant.

00:07:34.540 --> 00:07:36.430
But today is special.

00:07:36.650 --> 00:07:41.380
As Judge Man, I will administer justice in this duel!

00:07:42.480 --> 00:07:44.140
Judge Man?

00:07:44.710 --> 00:07:46.770
You keep changing appearances!

00:07:46.770 --> 00:07:49.250
You even pretended to be Mai.

00:07:49.250 --> 00:07:52.240
I really thought she woke up.

00:07:52.620 --> 00:07:53.880
I won't forgive you.

00:07:54.170 --> 00:07:56.820
I'll never forgive you!

00:07:58.310 --> 00:08:02.930
The defendant Katsuya Jonouchi, build your deck.

00:08:03.900 --> 00:08:05.400
R-Right!

00:08:06.820 --> 00:08:07.530
Okay.

00:08:07.920 --> 00:08:09.970
This.  And this.

00:08:10.200 --> 00:08:11.300
And...

00:08:11.720 --> 00:08:17.800
Katsuya Jonouchi, my research says that you'll build a Gamble Deck.

00:08:20.960 --> 00:08:22.850
I'm ready, Judge!

00:08:23.140 --> 00:08:28.850
Good.  Pick one card in your deck to be your Deck Master.

00:08:28.850 --> 00:08:31.100
Oh yeah.  Hmm...

00:08:34.260 --> 00:08:35.900
Flame Swordsman.

00:08:36.240 --> 00:08:41.030
We've fought together many times.  I can trust this monster.

00:08:44.280 --> 00:08:47.900
It's perfect for my Deck Master.

00:08:47.900 --> 00:08:51.840
All right!  My Deck Master is Flame Swordsman!

00:08:55.760 --> 00:08:58.100
I'm counting on you, Flame Swordsman.

00:08:58.100 --> 00:09:00.450
Tell me your Deck Master ability.

00:09:01.020 --> 00:09:08.860
My Deck Master ability lets me give my attack points to Warrior-Type monsters in 100-point increments.

00:09:10.680 --> 00:09:14.260
As you can see, my Deck Master is Judge Man.

00:09:15.770 --> 00:09:18.130
The duel will now begin!

00:09:25.350 --> 00:09:27.610
My turn.  I draw.

00:09:27.900 --> 00:09:30.240
I summon Hysteric Fairy!

00:09:35.310 --> 00:09:38.560
That monster irritates me.

00:09:38.560 --> 00:09:40.460
1800 attack points?

00:09:40.810 --> 00:09:43.390
I leave it in attack position and end my turn.

00:09:43.800 --> 00:09:45.250
Here I go!  My turn!

00:09:45.250 --> 00:09:46.080
I draw!

00:09:46.480 --> 00:09:48.460
Gearfried the Iron Knight.

00:09:49.150 --> 00:09:52.270
Its attack points are the same as his monster.

00:09:52.550 --> 00:09:56.440
Okay!  I'll use my Deck Master's ability.

00:09:57.870 --> 00:10:00.370
I summon Gearfried the Iron Knight!

00:10:02.950 --> 00:10:07.570
With my Deck Master's ability, it gains 500 attack points!

00:10:08.500 --> 00:10:09.350
Here I go!

00:10:09.350 --> 00:10:11.670
Gearfried the Iron Knight attacks!

00:10:11.670 --> 00:10:14.000
Destroy Hysteric Fairy!

00:10:22.350 --> 00:10:24.970
Good!  I end my turn!

00:10:26.000 --> 00:10:31.950
He already used his Deck Master's ability.  He learned the rules quickly.

00:10:32.330 --> 00:10:34.410
My turn.  I draw.

00:10:34.800 --> 00:10:38.850
I set this monster and end my turn.

00:10:38.850 --> 00:10:41.200
My turn.  I draw.

00:10:42.270 --> 00:10:45.290
I know that monster has a Flip Effect.

00:10:45.650 --> 00:10:48.300
But that doesn't scare me.

00:10:49.220 --> 00:10:51.310
I'll keep going!

00:10:53.340 --> 00:10:55.830
I summon Little-Winguard!

00:10:57.140 --> 00:10:58.620
My Deck Master's ability!

00:10:59.310 --> 00:11:01.940
It gains 300 attack points!

00:11:02.940 --> 00:11:06.600
Little-Winguard attacks the set monster!

00:11:12.540 --> 00:11:15.080
Skelengel's Flip Effect activates.

00:11:15.080 --> 00:11:16.750
I draw a card.

00:11:17.080 --> 00:11:19.450
You have no monsters left.

00:11:19.850 --> 00:11:20.740
Here I go!

00:11:20.740 --> 00:11:22.960
Gearfried attacks you directly!

00:11:29.110 --> 00:11:31.650
N-Not bad.

00:11:32.080 --> 00:11:33.310
How's that?

00:11:33.310 --> 00:11:36.340
See how skilled I am?

00:11:36.340 --> 00:11:40.510
You're not good enough to defeat me.

00:11:40.510 --> 00:11:43.200
Come back when you've improved!

00:11:46.220 --> 00:11:48.520
Enjoy this while you can.

00:11:48.740 --> 00:11:53.740
In gambling theory, you must make your opponent feel confident.

00:11:54.020 --> 00:11:56.360
C'mon!  It's your turn!

00:11:56.360 --> 00:12:01.680
So when he loses, the fall will be even greater.

00:12:03.600 --> 00:12:04.800
I draw.

00:12:05.360 --> 00:12:08.270
I summon Mystical Elf in defense position.

00:12:08.620 --> 00:12:12.610
I set one card and end my turn.

00:12:18.250 --> 00:12:20.760
Playtime is over.

00:12:20.760 --> 00:12:23.110
Time to get serious.

00:12:41.680 --> 00:12:43.840
So cold...

00:12:44.950 --> 00:12:45.750
Here.

00:12:46.850 --> 00:12:48.830
Thanks Yugi, but-

00:12:48.830 --> 00:12:50.750
I wonder if everyone's okay?

00:12:52.640 --> 00:12:55.120
I bet they're forced to duel, too.

00:12:55.340 --> 00:13:01.860
Save Kaiba and Jonouchi, Shizuka and Honda are beginners when it comes to dueling.

00:13:02.200 --> 00:13:03.020
Yeah.

00:13:03.320 --> 00:13:06.460
Honda's dueling instincts are horrible!

00:13:06.820 --> 00:13:08.460
Ah-choo!

00:13:09.200 --> 00:13:10.570
Are you okay?

00:13:10.570 --> 00:13:12.530
I'm fine.

00:13:12.530 --> 00:13:14.700
Don't get Shizuka sick.

00:13:14.700 --> 00:13:16.030
I'm not sick!

00:13:16.030 --> 00:13:18.140
Someone's gossiping about me.

00:13:18.970 --> 00:13:23.080
Does Shizuka even know the rules of dueling?

00:13:23.370 --> 00:13:24.220
Ah-choo.

00:13:25.000 --> 00:13:27.050
She caught your cold!

00:13:27.050 --> 00:13:28.700
Stay away from her!

00:13:28.700 --> 00:13:30.420
What's with you, Otogi?

00:13:30.420 --> 00:13:32.510
I'll get you sick, too!

00:13:32.510 --> 00:13:37.140
Cough cough!

00:13:37.140 --> 00:13:38.770
Stop it!

00:13:38.770 --> 00:13:39.630
Cough cough!

00:13:39.970 --> 00:13:43.680
We must find them fast!  Shizuka may be in trouble!

00:13:43.680 --> 00:13:44.970
Let's hurry, Yugi.

00:13:44.970 --> 00:13:45.630
Yeah.

00:13:48.520 --> 00:13:49.610
Damn.

00:13:49.610 --> 00:13:52.110
How big is this forest?

00:13:52.400 --> 00:13:54.550
Noa, just wait.

00:13:54.550 --> 00:13:59.050
I'll escape from this lame virtual world and drag you out!

00:13:59.960 --> 00:14:02.740
You want to leave the forest that badly?

00:14:02.740 --> 00:14:04.420
As you wish.

00:14:11.890 --> 00:14:12.910
Big brother.

00:14:20.270 --> 00:14:21.300
This place...

00:14:23.550 --> 00:14:26.240
Kaiba Corporation's president's office!

00:14:27.080 --> 00:14:28.680
What do you want?

00:14:29.020 --> 00:14:29.840
What?

00:14:32.570 --> 00:14:34.080
Gozaburo.

00:14:34.370 --> 00:14:38.720
It's about the virtual system that I developed.

00:14:38.720 --> 00:14:41.260
Big brother, this is virtual footage.

00:14:42.110 --> 00:14:43.510
I remember this.

00:14:43.510 --> 00:14:47.690
This occurred two years before I became president of Kaiba Corporation.

00:14:48.220 --> 00:14:50.630
There's nothing to talk about.

00:14:50.840 --> 00:14:53.200
Seto, I'm busy.

00:14:53.200 --> 00:14:54.070
Leave.

00:14:54.480 --> 00:14:59.010
I developed that system so that everyone can enjoy playing games!

00:14:59.300 --> 00:15:02.850
But you're using it for war, Father!

00:15:04.160 --> 00:15:07.240
Didn't you hear that I told you to leave?

00:15:07.360 --> 00:15:09.400
It's not a tool for war!

00:15:09.400 --> 00:15:12.480
It's for Kaiba Land that I'm planning to build-

00:15:13.110 --> 00:15:14.920
I told you to leave!

00:15:15.260 --> 00:15:16.750
Kaiba Land?

00:15:17.350 --> 00:15:18.710
Such nonsense!

00:15:19.020 --> 00:15:22.830
Making stupid games isn't a worthwhile job!

00:15:23.020 --> 00:15:25.450
Listen closely, Seto.

00:15:25.450 --> 00:15:29.000
The Kaiba family's heir must be a king who rules the world!

00:15:29.000 --> 00:15:32.710
My goal is to rule the world as a defense contractor!

00:15:32.980 --> 00:15:38.100
With your virtual system, I'll redraw the world map!

00:15:38.260 --> 00:15:39.810
You're wrong, Father!

00:15:42.550 --> 00:15:43.720
Let me go!

00:15:44.020 --> 00:15:45.050
Let me go!

00:15:45.050 --> 00:15:46.720
We're not done talking!

00:15:46.720 --> 00:15:48.970
Father!

00:15:49.510 --> 00:15:53.910
After that day, I never called him "Father" again.

00:16:01.180 --> 00:16:09.800
He wanted to use my virtual system to make tons of money in exchange for many people dying in war.

00:16:09.800 --> 00:16:13.580
I couldn't let someone that filthy have my system.

00:16:14.080 --> 00:16:16.880
I decided to forsake him that day.

00:16:16.880 --> 00:16:21.020
I was more determined to take over Kaiba Corporation.

00:16:21.350 --> 00:16:22.700
Big brother...

00:16:23.300 --> 00:16:32.400
Anyway, Noa is having fun intruding into my memories and watching my reactions.

00:16:32.400 --> 00:16:34.400
Unforgivable!

00:16:34.820 --> 00:16:36.070
Listen, Noah!

00:16:36.360 --> 00:16:42.880
Your sleazy mind must be planning to take over Kaiba Corporation!

00:16:43.250 --> 00:16:44.540
But I won't let you!

00:16:44.800 --> 00:16:49.820
I'll completely crush your plans!

00:16:50.570 --> 00:16:53.640
Take over Kaiba Corporation?

00:17:00.620 --> 00:17:02.800
My turn!  I draw!

00:17:03.380 --> 00:17:06.330
He only has one monster on his field.

00:17:06.760 --> 00:17:09.000
That set card worries me.

00:17:10.000 --> 00:17:11.380
But I'm a man.

00:17:11.380 --> 00:17:12.960
I'm going for it!

00:17:12.960 --> 00:17:15.400
Rocket Warrior in attack position!

00:17:17.910 --> 00:17:20.600
How's that!  Scared?

00:17:20.600 --> 00:17:22.250
It's over for you.

00:17:22.250 --> 00:17:27.990
My three monsters will blow away your weak defending monster!

00:17:28.220 --> 00:17:31.160
And attack you directly for victory!

00:17:31.570 --> 00:17:33.080
Go, Gearfried!

00:17:33.080 --> 00:17:34.760
Attack Mystical Elf!

00:17:35.040 --> 00:17:37.430
I activate my Deck Master's ability!

00:17:37.660 --> 00:17:39.820
Oh no!  I forgot about that!

00:17:39.820 --> 00:17:42.870
He also has a Deck Master ability!

00:17:44.500 --> 00:17:47.560
You're so naive.

00:17:47.560 --> 00:17:51.600
My Deck Master's ability is perfect for you.

00:17:52.860 --> 00:17:54.250
Life Sentence!

00:17:54.460 --> 00:17:57.680
Life Sentence?  What's that?

00:17:58.040 --> 00:18:02.120
By paying 1000 life points, the decision is overturned!

00:18:02.400 --> 00:18:06.560
All monsters on your field are banished!

00:18:06.780 --> 00:18:08.000
What?  No way!

00:18:08.000 --> 00:18:10.820
Wait!  Is this for real?

00:18:14.430 --> 00:18:20.510
Furthermore, you take 500 points of damage for every banished monster.

00:18:20.720 --> 00:18:22.420
Say what?

00:18:22.700 --> 00:18:26.080
I lost three monsters, so...

00:18:26.410 --> 00:18:28.660
I lose 1500 life points?

00:18:28.660 --> 00:18:30.250
Well done.

00:18:30.250 --> 00:18:31.700
Damn!

00:18:32.740 --> 00:18:35.650
But it's not a big deal.

00:18:35.650 --> 00:18:38.110
He only has 200 life points.

00:18:38.110 --> 00:18:39.570
I'll win easily.

00:18:42.420 --> 00:18:44.340
Bottomless Trap Hole.

00:18:44.680 --> 00:18:50.910
If he summons, Flip Summons or Special Summons a monster with 1500-or-more attack points...

00:18:50.910 --> 00:18:54.140
...this trap card destroys and banishes that monster.

00:18:54.510 --> 00:19:00.150
I bet he's going to tribute Mystical Elf to summon a high-Level monster.

00:19:00.150 --> 00:19:02.080
But I'll have this trap ready.

00:19:03.050 --> 00:19:04.020
Perfect!

00:19:04.840 --> 00:19:06.380
I set one card!

00:19:06.730 --> 00:19:08.450
I end my turn!

00:19:13.860 --> 00:19:15.100
Yugi, look!

00:19:15.100 --> 00:19:16.560
There's a door!

00:19:17.240 --> 00:19:19.420
You're right.  Let's go!

00:19:24.890 --> 00:19:26.120
Hey guys!

00:19:26.120 --> 00:19:27.110
Jonouchi?

00:19:27.210 --> 00:19:28.270
Jonouchi?

00:19:28.480 --> 00:19:32.010
Yugi!  Anzu!  You're both OK!

00:19:32.710 --> 00:19:36.480
Silence!  Visitors must take a seat!

00:19:37.170 --> 00:19:37.650
Right.

00:19:37.970 --> 00:19:40.330
You came at the right time!

00:19:40.330 --> 00:19:43.090
Watch me defeat him!

00:19:43.400 --> 00:19:46.020
I'm resuming the duel.  I draw!

00:19:49.700 --> 00:19:53.860
Jonouchi has no monsters, and it's the opponent's turn.

00:19:53.860 --> 00:19:55.130
Is he OK?

00:19:55.440 --> 00:19:57.800
I summon Curtain of the Dark Ones!

00:20:00.810 --> 00:20:02.650
I flip over my set card.

00:20:02.650 --> 00:20:04.250
Polymerization!

00:20:05.170 --> 00:20:11.340
I fuse Mystical Elf and Curtain of the Dark Ones to summon Kamionwizard!

00:20:13.310 --> 00:20:17.110
Once it's summoned, it'll fall into Bottomless Trap Hole.

00:20:21.500 --> 00:20:23.730
Only 1300 attack points.

00:20:23.730 --> 00:20:27.330
This trap doesn't activate unless it has at least 1500 points.

00:20:27.330 --> 00:20:31.270
I activate the Continuous Spell, Sinister Justice!

00:20:31.480 --> 00:20:36.340
Level 4-and-below Fusion Monsters can attack on the turn it's summoned.

00:20:36.600 --> 00:20:41.150
Kamionwizard, attack Katsuya Jonouchi directly!

00:20:45.030 --> 00:20:46.530
Jonouchi!

00:20:54.370 --> 00:20:56.730
Sinister Justice.

00:20:57.620 --> 00:21:02.650
When a Level 4-or-below Fusion Monster deals damage...

00:21:02.650 --> 00:21:06.700
...that Continuous Spell gives him 800 life points.

00:21:06.860 --> 00:21:08.150
What?

00:21:09.460 --> 00:21:10.680
Correct.

00:21:14.080 --> 00:21:15.340
And...

00:21:15.560 --> 00:21:19.120
I set one card and end my turn.

00:21:20.020 --> 00:21:22.840
He regained life points.

00:21:22.840 --> 00:21:26.060
Just when I was about to defeat him.

00:21:45.280 --> 00:21:52.170
Judge Man's Deck Master ability and Continuous Spells have turned the tables on Jonouchi.

00:21:52.170 --> 00:21:55.800
He's fighting back with his specialty - Gamble Cards.

00:21:55.800 --> 00:22:00.140
But they all backfire, putting him in more trouble!

00:22:00.140 --> 00:22:03.060
Jonouchi is depressed that luck has forsaken him.

00:22:03.060 --> 00:22:05.310
But something's weird about his misses!

00:22:05.310 --> 00:22:07.570
Next time on Yu-Gi-Oh!:
Gamble For Victory

00:22:07.570 --> 00:22:09.080
Duel, standby!

00:22:13.890 --> 00:22:21.790
The sun never sets
It rises forever

00:22:21.790 --> 00:22:30.740
Don't let a dream end as a dream

00:22:31.070 --> 00:22:35.710
The straight rail and harsh route

00:22:35.710 --> 00:22:39.680
Whether to go or not 
all of yourself

00:22:40.110 --> 00:22:47.650
I'm tired of counting on my fingers inside this cage

00:22:47.650 --> 00:22:51.220
Respect! Boys  Show me how you act tough

00:22:51.220 --> 00:22:55.990
Draw a map, even if it's sloppy

00:22:55.990 --> 00:23:06.100
And walk it without stopping

00:23:06.100 --> 00:23:13.710
The sun never sets
If I can be like you

00:23:13.940 --> 00:23:22.680
Create freedom by exceeding common ideas

00:23:22.680 --> 00:23:30.660
I want to trust myself
Sometimes I'll lose my way but

00:23:30.660 --> 00:23:40.500
I hide it in my heart...
Secret Paradise
